WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.649
Solo: A Star Wars Story has arrived in theaters,
and it finally answers all sorts of questions

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:11.040
fans have been asking for decades like how
Han and Chewie first met, how Han really won

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.179
the Millennium Falcon from Lando, and what
really happened during the infamous Kessel

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:16.179
Run.

00:00:16.179 --> 00:00:20.180
But for every long-held Star Wars riddle the
film answered, it may have actually posed

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.720
even more new questions.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.970
Here's a spoiler-filled look at the biggest
unanswered questions in Solo: A Star Wars

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.560
Story.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.290
What's Qi'ra hiding?

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.730
When Han is finally reunited with his long-lost
love Qi'ra, it should be a joyous occasion.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:38.720
But it isn't, because Qi'ra is clearly hiding
something or many things from her one-time

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.720
boyfriend.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.190
The question is: what exactly is she hiding?

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.210
It's telling that when Han asks her how she
got out, she says she never did.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:50.390
Between her comments about owing the Crimson
Dawn a major debt and Tobias Beckett's frequent

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:55.370
hints that Qi'ra has done unspeakable things,
it's clear there's a lot more to her story.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:00.129
But until and unless we get a sequel, it seems
we'll just have to wonder exactly what Qi'ra

00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:05.160
had to do to get off of Corellia that has
her so indebted to a guy like Darth Maul.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.160
Speaking of which…

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.250
Wait, Darth Maul?!

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.360
Probably the most shocking moment in Solo
was the surprise reveal that Darth Maul is

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.590
the head honcho of the evil Crimson Dawn crime
syndicate.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.270
Part of the reason it was such a surprise
is that the last time moviegoers saw Maul,

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:23.580
he had just been literally chopped in half
in 1999's The Phantom Menace.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:28.110
Apparently, he got better, something fans
of the Star Wars cartoons already knew.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:33.050
In Clone Wars and Rebels, it was established
that he used the force to survive his bisecting,

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:37.490
got some robot legs, and eventually ended
his life in a very brief and poorly thought

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.330
out attempt to get revenge on Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.720
So what does Maul's appearance mean for any
possible Solo sequels?

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.820
Are we going to get to see a throwdown between
Maul and Han?

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.080
Is Qi-ra going to become Maul's apprentice?

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.250
We can't wait to find out!

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.970
What about the Wookiees?

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:57.220
After Chewbacca is rescued from slavery, he
explains in a heartbreaking sequence that

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.150
all the Wookiees were enslaved and driven
from their home world, and he's on a quest

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.150
to find them.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:05.770
But when he does finally find some of his
fellow Wookiees, after helping them escape

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.130
from bondage he just… kinda leaves.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.970
That opens up all sorts of questions.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.520
Who exactly are these other Wookiees?

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.910
Fans had speculated that they might be his
wife Malla and his son Lumpy, first seen in

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:22.270
the 1978 Star Wars Holiday Special, but since
there are no subtitles, we don't actually

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:27.720
find out whether or not they're Chewie's family,
his tribe, or just some fuzzy randos.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.780
Where do they go and what happens to them
when Chewbacca leaves?

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.890
Why does Chewie decide to stick with Han instead
of his people?

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.730
What role do the Wookiees play going forward?

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.340
We've got a lot of questions about the Wookiees.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.300
But so far, only Chewie knows the answer and
if he's telling us, we sure don't understand

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:42.800
it.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.360
"That's yes."

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.220
What happened to L3?

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:53.360
Arguably the biggest breakout character in
Solo is Lando's first mate, navigator, and

00:02:53.370 --> 00:03:00.460
possible love interest L337 . So when L3 tragically
dies during the slave uprising she incited,

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.569
it's both moving and oddly triumphant.

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:06.350
And then they take part of her brain and upload
it into the Millennium Falcon, with Lando

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.550
declaring she's now part of the ship.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.960
Sooo… that leaves us with a bunch of questions.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:16.340
Does this mean L3 is actually in the Falcon
throughout the rest of the Star Wars series?

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:20.490
Is it possible that at some point between
Solo and A New Hope, Lando and the gang are

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:25.220
able to extract L3's consciousness from the
Falcon and give her a body again - maybe even

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.510
a human body in the form of Lando's cyborg
partner Lobot?

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:33.370
And considering her entire deal was trying
to free droids from subservience, isn't it

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:37.060
really unfortunate that she ends up just being
turned into a mindless tool?

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.840
Here's hoping we get L3 back somehow in the
future.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.930
Did Enfys Nest start the rebellion?

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.800
At the end of Solo, Enfys Nest the leader
of the so-called outlaw gang that's been dogging

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:52.410
Tobias Beckett throughout the film tells Han
that she's going to use the millions of credits

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:57.250
from the stolen shipment of coaxium to fund
a rebellion to fight against the Empire.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.980
This bombshell seems to suggest that Enfys
Nest is actually the founder of the Rebel

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:02.980
Alliance!

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:06.620
But if Enfys Nest did actually start the Rebellion,
what happened to her?

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.750
Could she somehow be related to Rey?

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.450
And if Han was in on the ground floor of creating
the Rebellion, how come this never came up

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:16.570
before - like when he later became a Rebel
General in Return of the Jedi?

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:20.489
Here's hoping we get to learn a lot more about
Enfys Nest in the future.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:21.720
And speaking of the future...

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.720
Now what?

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.660
In April of 2018, Solo star Alden Ehrenreich
revealed that he was under contract for three

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.660
films.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.060
And it seems clear that Solo is setting things
up for a trilogy or more.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:36.880
With major plot threads around the Crimson
Dawn, Qi-ra, and Darth Maul left dangling,

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:41.610
not to mention the fate of L3, the Wookiees
and the birth of the Rebellion, Solo seems

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:45.639
prepared to fill in the gaps of everything
that happened between Revenge of the Sith

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:46.639
and A New Hope.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:49.170
But will Solo actually get a sequel?

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:53.530
All of it comes down to how much money Solo
makes, meaning the answer to that question,

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:56.639
and all the rest, can actually be found right
now in your wallet.

00:04:56.639 --> 00:04:57.720
Thanks for watching!

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.389
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:02.389
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

